  era: "Section 30 \xB7 Constitution of India \xB7 1946 \u2013 present"
  title: Directive Principles of State Policy
  text: 'Part Four sets out Directive Principles of State Policy: goals of social and economic justice, such as adequate livelihood, equal pay for equal work, education and village panchayats. They cannot be enforced in court but are fundamental to governance.'
